# Public/Private Boundary (Telegram Model)

Architecture: open client + open transport + private core.
Follow `docs/ai-boundary-policy.md`.

## Layer rules
- `api/v1/` routes must NOT contain `select()`, `session.execute()`,
  or direct ORM queries. All DB access goes through services/repos.
- `services/` import decision functions from `dotsound_private_core`.
- Security constants (TTLs, attempt limits, cooldowns) -> PrivateCore.
- Decision functions (should_burn, is_internal_ip) -> PrivateCore.
- Anti-abuse logic (disposable email, Tor, moderation) -> PrivateCore.
- Redis/DB/HTTP orchestration -> Backend adapter.
- When adding new auth/abuse logic: add rules to PrivateCore first,
  then import in Backend. Never hardcode thresholds locally.
- Frontend builds independently (`npm run build`). It talks to
  Backend only through `/api/v1/` REST and WebSocket.
- If a request can cross boundaries and intent is unclear, stop and ask.

